      `s.as_bytes().ends_with(suffix.as_bytes())` — not the C source
      directly when running under `bin/simple test` (tree-walk
      interpreter). Both the interpreter shim and the C source at
      runtime_native.c:3670-3675 implement the identical contract (empty
      suffix -> true; suffix longer than subject -> false; otherwise a
      byte-wise tail comparison via memcmp/`.ends_with`), so this spec
      differentially compares against whichever is actually reached by the
